# A2/A2.1/A2_09_home_and_furniture.letz
# Source: L07.md (A2.1 Conversatioun, Lektioun 7: säin Doheem beschreiwen).
# All vocabulary lemmas were verified against LOD; the source's “Zännbüscht” was
# standardized to LOD's “Zännbiischt”. A1 vocabulary is deliberately not repeated
# as new Elements; it returns in the sentences as support for the new home words.
# Grammar focus: all fourteen changing prepositions take dative articles with a
# static verb and accusative articles with a movement verb. The fills isolate both
# the preposition and its article, and distinguish hänken / stoen / leien by use.

@lesson A2.09 "Home & Furniture"

# --- Rooms and furniture ---
@word d'Kachmaschinn = the cooker
@word d'Handduch = the hand towel
@word d'Bild = the picture
@word den Nuetsdësch = the bedside table
@word d'Zännbiischt = the toothbrush
@word d'Kachplack = the hob
@word d'Kaffismaschinn = the coffee machine
@word d'Kaffismillen = the coffee grinder
@word den Uewen = the oven
@word de Kicheschaf = the kitchen cupboard
@word de Kleederschaf = the wardrobe

@sentence
@lu Ech wunnen an engem Appartement zu Miersch.
@en I live in an apartment in Mersch.
@distractor-en house
@distractor-en work
@distractor-lu Haus
@distractor-lu schaffen

@sentence
@lu Meng Wunneng huet eng Kichen, eng Stuff an e Schlofzëmmer.
@en My apartment has a kitchen, a living room, and a bedroom.
@distractor-en bathroom
@distractor-en garden
@distractor-lu Buedzëmmer
@distractor-lu Gaart

@sentence
@lu An der Kichen steet eng Kachmaschinn.
@en There is a cooker in the kitchen.
@distractor-en fridge
@distractor-en bathroom
@distractor-lu Frigo
@distractor-lu Buedzëmmer

@sentence
@lu Op der Kachplack steet en Dëppen.
@en A pot stands on the hob.
@distractor-en plate
@distractor-en chair
@distractor-lu Teller
@distractor-lu Stull

@sentence
